      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="824764260">
          <groundspeak:date>2019-01-12T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1636194">behmSquad</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP461 Morley Boundary #36 (Found)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I found myself on Sibbald Creek Trail heading for a newly published nearby challenge when I looked at my gps and noticed there was a cap just a little further up the hill.  So glad that I went to the trouble of loading all the caps onto my gps; I would have missed this one otherwise.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="729884615">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-10-27T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP461 Morley [FOUND].  Out on a fall hike along Pine Top ridge.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="408529953">
          <groundspeak:date>2014-05-17T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3073571">GeoMonkey_AB</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP 461 - Morley Boundary #36

N51 02.759 W114 43.889&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We made our way up the ridge to collect Pine Top #2 and decided to continue on to this one. I never thought I'd ever see this rather remote section of the Morley boundary but caching takes you to some interesting places! Thanks for the cap - possibly the cleanest I have ever seen.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="408406641">
          <groundspeak:date>2014-05-17T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="325658">kristaandgeoff</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP461 Morley Boundary #36&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;N 51 02.759 W 114 43.887&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While doing some hiking in the area with GeoMonkey_AB we managed to grab this one. I volunteered to go get it, as you do have to cross the fence (for about a metre) to get the pictures. This is probably the cap in the best condition that I've seen yet. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
